SUMMARY:Quand la terre respire: A multimedia installation by Sarah Abdel-J
 elil '16
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Hamlin Creative Space\;\n(one floor directly below Kracum Perform
 ance Hall)\;\nWeitz Center for Creativity\;\n320 3rd Street East\, Northfi
 eld\, MN 55057
DESCRIPTION:Quand la terre respire ("when the earth breathes") is a multim
 edia installation drawing from the artist's nomadic upbringing\, fractal g
 eometry\, Islamic art and design\, pattern\, dance\, repetition\, and the 
 oscillation between personal and geological time. Artist\, Sarah Abdel-Jel
 il\, graduated from Carleton in 2016 with a degree in Cinema and Media Stu
 dies.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.car
 leton.edu/_c/ut7X
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton Arts Calendar":mailto:m3mgdme4j7u3ame5pt83faap1g@gr
 oup.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260825T192903
END:VEVENT
