TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Multicultural Center
DESCRIPTION:<div class="gmail_default">\n\nJoin us for games\, food\, and 
 good conversation with other BIPOC students!\n\nLunch is provided\, and re
 gistration is not required.\n\nThe <a href="https://www.carleton.edu/bipoc
 mhc/">BIPOC Mental Health Collective</a> (BIPOC MHC) at Carleton College 
 provides a community for Black Indigenous and People of Color students to 
 engage in restorative practices that support their mental health and well-
 being. The BIPOC MHC is led by staff from <a href="https://www.carleton.e
 du/student-health/">Student Health and Counseling</a> and the <a href="h
 ttps://www.carleton.edu/oil/">Office of Intercultural Life</a>. Contact <a
  href="https://www.carleton.edu/directory/lbaquerooja/">Lucy Baquero Oja</
 a> to be added to our Google group.\n\n</div>\n\nView this event on the C
 arleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut7L
