UID:lu0v2f3gab5gna4b22rp7gaen0
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T045925
DTSTART:20260924T150000
DTEND:20260924T160000
SUMMARY:Carl Talks: Public Media Under Pressure — Leading MPR News Throu
 gh Minnesota's Most Consequential Years with Stephanie Curtis '92
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:virtual
DESCRIPTION:<h3 style="text-align: center">Carl Talks\n<em><b>\n</b></em>P
 ublic Media Under Pressure — Leading MPR News Through Minnesota's Most C
 onsequential Years\nwith Stephanie Curtis '92</h3>\n<h4 style="text-align:
  center">Thursday\, September 24\, 2026\n3 p.m. Central Time\nvia Zoom</h4
 >\n<div>\n<div><img class="alignright" src="https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploa
 ds/sites/736/2026/09/image001.png?resize=480\,480" alt="" width="217" heig
 ht="217" data-name="image" />As federal funding cuts reshape the future of
  public media\, Stephanie Curtis '92 will discuss what's at stake for loca
 l journalism and the communities it serves. She'll draw on her experience 
 leading the MPR News team through five of the most consequential years in 
 Minnesota news to talk about what it takes to keep a newsroom steady throu
 gh political and financial upheaval.</div>\n<strong>Stephanie Curtis '92</
 strong> is the director of programming for MPR News. Her career at MPR beg
 an as an intern on the local All Things Considered. She’s produced call-
 in shows\, ideas festivals\, a literary series\, and was a founding staff 
 member of The Current. The MPR News audience knows her best as the Movie M
 aven. Stephanie currently lives in the city where she was born\, St. Paul\
 , with her husband (Carleton ’94.)\n\n</div>\n<a href="https://www.alumn
 iq.carleton.edu/index.cfm/events:register/home/eventId/542"><strong>Regist
 er</strong> </a><strong>by Wednesday\, September 23 </strong>to participat
 e in this Zoom event.\n\n<strong>Cost:</strong> None.\n\nUnable to join ou
 r live event? No problem — we will post a recording of the event on our 
 <a href="https://www.carleton.edu/alumni/news/recordings/"><strong>Alumni 
 Events Recordings</strong></a> page.\n\n<strong>Questions?</strong> Conta
 ct Alumni Relations via <a href="mailto:alumni-office@carleton.edu?subject
 =Carleton%20event%20question"><strong>email</strong></a> or 800-729-2586.\
 n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.
 edu/_c/uubZ
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton’s Regional Carls Program":mailto:r7km2dafnqvrponn
 mp387i2vgg@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260909T175215
END:VEVENT
