SUMMARY:Artist Talk: Michelle Gregor
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Boliou 104
DESCRIPTION:<em>This talk is sponsored by the Mary Leigh Miller Fund for C
 eramics with support from the Gender\, Women's and Sexuality Studies Progr
 am</em>\n\nMichelle Gregor is an American sculptor\, painter and arts educ
 ator\, based in the San Francisco Bay Area. Focusing on the abstract human
  figure in ceramic\, Gregor's forms apply the free\, intuitive impulses of
  Abstract Expressionism to figurative representation.\nGregor's talk coinc
 ides with an exhibition of work at the Northern Clay Center's exhibition <
 a href="https://northernclaycenter.org/2026/07/31/to-be-human/">To Be Huma
 n</a>\, curated by Professor Kelly Connole. This exhibition will run Sept 
 19 through Nov 1\, 2026.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College websit
 e:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuh3
ORGANIZER;CN="Art & Art History":mailto:8ckv8vtit6m6sj5p1qnvn5qq14@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260903T174353
END:VEVENT
