SUMMARY:Sukkot Shabbat Service
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Chapel Lawn (Rain Location: AGH)
DESCRIPTION:Sukkot is a week-long Jewish holiday celebrating the harvest a
 nd God's protection during the period of time ancient Jews spent in exile 
 after leaving Egypt. This year Sukkot is celebrated from September 25 to O
 ctober 2. Part of this holiday is the building of the sukkah\, a temporary
  shelter that is often used as a place to eat and reside in during observa
 nce of Sukkot.\n\nThe Sukkot Shabbat Service will be led by Rav Michaela B
 rown. Cohost JSC.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhtt
 ps://www.carleton.edu/_c/utYn
ORGANIZER;CN="Chaplain's Office":mailto:gc0r4cojm5g3aensafau0dppd8@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260605T190759
END:VEVENT
