SUMMARY:Arboretum Centennial Speaker Series:  Reimagining Restoration\, Da
 n Hernández and Mark McKone of the Carleton Biology Department
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz 236 (please enter on the 320 Third Street East entrance)
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for the first presentation of the Arboretum's C
 entennial Speaker Series\, <em>Reimagining Restoration</em> with Carleton 
 Professors of Biology\, <a href="https://www.carleton.edu/directory/hernan
 dez/">Dan Hernández</a> and <a href="https://www.carleton.edu/directory/m
 mckone/">Mark Mckone.</a> This event will be held in Weitz 236. Please ent
 er on the 320 Third Street East entrance. \n\nThe restoration of native ec
 ological communities has been a focus of activity in Carleton's Cowling Ar
 boretum since its founding a century ago. Early efforts focused on forest 
 habitats\, but in the last 50 years there also have been large plantings o
 f tallgrass prairies. The traditional goal of prairie restoration has been
  to return these ecosystems to their perceived historic state. But the rea
 lity of global environmental changes requires us to reconsider strategies 
 for effective prairie restoration and management. We will review the histo
 ry of prairie restoration in the Arboretum\, and discuss a new project tha
 t considers how to make restored prairies more resilient to future climate
  change by sourcing seeds from locations that more closely match the curre
 nt and projected future climate of the Arb.\n\nView this event on the Carl
 eton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuh5
ORGANIZER;CN="Cowling Arboretum":mailto:arsa1npokgd6u28r3pibqv644s@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260813T193101
END:VEVENT
