DTSTART:20260929T114500
DTEND:20260929T130000
SUMMARY:Faculty-Led Research with Community Partners
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz 236
DESCRIPTION:<p class="p1"><strong>FACULTY-LED RESEARCH WITH COMMUNITY PART
 NERS</strong></p>\n<p class="p1">This session will invite a panel of facul
 ty to share about their community-engaged research\, how they prepare and 
 guide and transition students in and out of the ongoing projects\, and the
  benefitsto student learning and long-term partnerships.</p>\n<p class="p1
 ">Claire Kelling\, Assistant Professor of Statistics\nAmy Csizmar Dalal\, 
 Professor and Chair of Computer Science\nMeredith McCoy\, Associate Profes
 sor of American Studies and History\nBaird Jarman\, Professor of Art Histo
 ry\nMichael McNally\, John M. &amp\; Elizabeth W. Musser Professor of Reli
 gion\nEmily Seru\, Associate Director for Academic Civic Engagement and Sc
 holarship\, CCCE\nStudents are welcome to attend.</p>\n\nView this event o
