UID:3bd40aetlfpur31ctiqoh1gtik
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T045925
DTSTART:20260929T120000
DTEND:20260929T130000
SUMMARY:The University of Chicago Divinity School Information Session
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:For more information or to register\, see <a href="https://carlet
 on.joinhandshake.com/events/1984166/share_preview/">Handshake</a>
DESCRIPTION:<img src="https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploads/sites/676/2025/10/U
 Chicago.png" alt="" data-name="image" />\n<div class="gs">\n<div class=" "
 >\n<div id=":3fb" class="ii gt adO">\n<div id=":3fc" class="a3s aiL ">\n<d
 iv id="avWBGd-4606">\n<div><strong>Join a community of scholars and profes
 sionals who guide the public’s understanding of religion.</strong></div>
 \n<div>\n\nWant to dive more deeply into questions big and small about rel
 igion as a category and the religions of the world\, their history\, belie
 fs\, and practices? Eager to cultivate habits of thinking\, learning\, and
  communicating that will help you navigate a changing world?\n\n</div>\n<d
 iv>Students with backgrounds in fields across the humanities and social sc
 iences are invited to learn more about graduate study and leadership in re
 ligion at the University of Chicago Divinity School. Joined by Carleton al
 umna and current MDiv Student <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/gillian
 -applegate/">Gillian Applegate ’17</a>\, MA/PhD Alumnus and Assistant De
 an of Students <a href="https://divinity.uchicago.edu/directory/nathan-j-h
 ardy-0" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.g
 oogle.com/url?q=https://divinity.uchicago.edu/directory/nathan-j-hardy-0&a
 mp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1787252579161000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1_t4FZqrHLswVoXG
 VlIopU">Nathan J. Hardy</a> will share information about what makes the D
 ivinity School a distinctive community of learning\, in which graduates go
  on to further study in elite doctoral programs and law schools\, religiou
 s leadership\, and an array of careers in non-profit and business sectors.
 </div>\n<div></div>\n<div><strong>Programs offered:</strong></div>\n<div>\
 n<div>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Our <b>two-year</b> <span role="presentation"><a hre
 f="https://divinity.uchicago.edu/MDivprogram" target="_blank" rel="noopene
 r" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://divinity.uch
 icago.edu/MDivprogram&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1786725686000000&amp\;usg
 =AOvVaw3iFrKPtnr8TsUA8oXDOy8D">Master of Arts in Divinity (MA)</a></span>
  provides advanced training in the academic study of religion and adjacen
 t fields for students eager to build research and writing skills\, enhance
  language training\, and pursue intellectual depth in a robust and academi
 cally varied community. This program is ideal for students interested in d
 octoral study\, but inclusive of broad outcomes.</li>\n 	<li>\n<div role="
 presentation">\n\nOur <a href="https://divinity.uchicago.edu/MA-AMRS-prog
 rams" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.goo
 gle.com/url?q=https://divinity.uchicago.edu/MA-AMRS-programs&amp\;source=g
 mail&amp\;ust=1786725686000000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1R00Nk_NjSAVY1xCegIEB9">Mast
 er of Arts in Religious Studies (AMRS)</a> program provides a foundationa
 l course of study for students interested in the arts\, law\, medicine\, t
 echnology\, business\, and more who would benefit in their career goals fr
 om foundational training in the academic study of religion. This program c
 an be pursued intensely over <b>one-year or part-time over up to three ye
 ars</b>. It is not typically considered adequate for entry into PhD progra
 ms.\n\n</div></li>\n 	<li>Rooted in the Divinity School’s historic commi
 tment to the training of scholarly ministers\, today’s <a href="https:/
 /divinity.uchicago.edu/MDivprogram" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sa
 feredirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://divinity.uchicago.edu/
 MDivprogram&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1786725686000000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3iF
 rKPtnr8TsUA8oXDOy8D">Master of Divinity (MDiv)</a> program welcomes stud
 ents of many traditions—Jewish\, Muslim\, Buddhist\, Hindu\, Jain\, Conf
 ucian\, Christian\, and humanist—as they prepare for engagement in an ev
 er-increasing variety of contexts alongside students anticipating ordinati
 on and traditional vocations in religious community leadership. Through t
 his <b>three-year program</b> of study\, students develop foundations fo
 r religious leadership and engagement\, integrating reflective practice th
 rough scholarship in a cohort-driven model that balances classroom and fie
 ld education.</li>\n</ul>\nStudents interested in the Divinity School’s 
 PhD program should reach out directly to <a href="mailto:divinityadmissio
 ns@uchicago.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Nathan</a> to determine wh
 ether this or other information sessions are more appropriate.\n\n</div>\
 n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\nView this event on the 
 Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut6p
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260803T204702
END:VEVENT
