BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:bb1hindvklaptpagjaftgc7q5k
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T045925
DTSTART:20261004T190000
DTEND:20261004T210000
SUMMARY:BALA-BILA feat. Balla Kouyate and Matchume Zango
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Kracum Performance Hall\, Weitz Center for Creativity
DESCRIPTION:BALA-BILA brings together two African master musicians – <st
 rong>Balla Kouyate</strong> on balafon\, calabash\, bass guitar and voice\
 , and <strong>Matchume Zango</strong> on timbila\, mbira\, percussion and 
 voice – through a live concert framed as an intercultural musical conver
 sation between the two artists. Kouyate\, from the West African country of
  Mali\, and Zango\, from the East African country of Mozambique\, are lead
 ing exponents of their respective principal instruments\, BALAfon and timB
 ILA\, two world heritage instruments that are played together for the firs
 t time.\n\nThis living-room-style concert features Kouyate and Zango as co
 mposers and multi-instrumentalists sharing the joy\, beauty and complexity
  of their music but also provides a unique opportunity for the audience to
  get to know Kouyate and Zango as human beings\, artists\, ambassadors\, a
 nd global citizens as they explore their connection to each other\, their 
 art\, and their cultural patrimony.\n\nView this event on the Carleton Col
 lege website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut9U
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton Arts Calendar":mailto:m3mgdme4j7u3ame5pt83faap1g@gr
 oup.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260902T154702
END:VEVENT
