SUMMARY:Jesuit Volunteer Corps Tabling at Sayles
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:<a href="https://apps.carleton.edu/map/sayles/">Sayles Tables</a>
DESCRIPTION:<img class="" src="https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploads/sites/676/
 2025/10/Jesuit.jpg" alt="Jesuit Volunteer Corps Logo" width="329" height="
 128" data-name="image" />\n\n<strong>Join us in the movement for social ju
 stice. Apply to become a Jesuit Volunteer and be forever changed.</strong>
 \n\n<a href="https://jesuitvolunteers.org/"><strong>Jesuit Volunteer Corps
  (JVC)</strong></a> connects women and men with one or more years of volu
 nteer service that focus on the core values of community\, spirituality\, 
 simple living\, and social and ecological justice.\n\nBecoming a <a href=
 "https://info.jesuitvolunteers.org/onejourneytwopaths">Jesuit Volunteer (J
 V)</a> is a journey for anyone — across faiths and spiritual background
 s — looking to dedicate a year of their life to advancing social justice
 \, serving their community\, and putting their beliefs into action. JVs fi
 nd personal transformation through service to others\, permanently alterin
 g the way they see the world.\n\nJesuit Volunteers commit to a year of ser
 vice within agencies at the front line of creating social change. JVs live
  in an intentional community with one another\, while engaging in the valu
 es of spirituality\, simple living\, social justice\, and community.\n\nTh
 ey offer a transformational journey discovered via two paths - <a href="h
 ttps://www.jesuitvolunteers.org/">Jesuit Volunteer Corps</a> and <a href
 ="https://jvcnorthwest.org/">Jesuit Volunteer Corps Northwest</a>.\n\nStop
  by the tables at Sayles and talk with <a href="https://jesuitvolunteers.
 org/team/">Caro Woodard</a>\, Recruiter and former Jesuit Volunteer\, to l
 earn more about the program and service opportunities. <a href="https://ww
 w.carleton.edu/career/connect/news-events/events/?eId=ut7T">Sign up</a> to
  meet 1:1 to get your direct questions answered!\n\nView this event on the
  Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut7U
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260825T182434
END:VEVENT
