SUMMARY:Colorado College Social Action Institute Information Session
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:<a href="https://www.carleton.edu/map/agh" target="_blank">Alumni
  Guest House Meeting Room</a>\; For more information or to register\, see 
 <a href="https://carleton.joinhandshake.com/edu/events/1983928" target="_b
 lank">Handshake</a>
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://www.coloradocollege.edu/offices/summersession
 /CC-students/activist-institute.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img 
 src="https://d31kydh6n6r5j5.cloudfront.net/uploads/sites/676/2023/08/Color
 ado-College.png" alt="Colorado College Logo" data-name="image" /></a>\n<di
 v>\n\nCarleton College is partnering with Colorado College to promote its
  <a href="https://www.coloradocollege.edu/offices/summersession/CC-studen
 ts/activism-institute.html">Social Action Institute</a>. This opportunity 
 is offered to up to students interested in engaging in activist and/or adv
 ocacy-focused work focused on one of two tracks:\n<ul>\n 	<li><strong>Comm
 unity Organizing to Support Labor\, Tenant/Housing\, and Immigrant Rights<
 /strong> (campaign recruitment\, event planning\, op-ed writing\, policy 
 research\, public speaking\, criminal justice accountability\, case advoca
 cy).</li>\n 	<li><strong>Environmental Justice Organizing</strong> (commu
 nity organizing\, advocacy campaigns\, research).</li>\n 	<li><strong>Immi
 grant Detention Work and Movement Lawyering</strong> (working with attorne
 ys representing immigrants in detention\; research on immigrant detention 
 center conditions\; researching country conditions for legal cases).</li>\
 n</ul>\nStudents will engage in work that aims to confront escalating surv
 eillance and criminalization of BIPOC communities by collaborating directl
 y with community-based organizations in the US Southwest.\n\nJoin <a href
 ="https://www.coloradocollege.edu/basics/contact/directory/people/popkin_e
 ric_s.html"><strong>Eric Popkin</strong></a>\, Associate Professor\, Depar
 tment of Sociology and Director of Colorado College Action Institute\, and
  potentially previous interns\,\n\n<strong>Tony Brown ’27</strong>\, Eng
 lish\; <strong>Olivia Lyman ’27</strong>\, Linguistics\; <strong>Zoe T
 omlin ’27</strong>\, Psychology and Religion\; <strong>Melissa Uc ’27
 </strong>\, History and Middle East Studies\; <strong>Sara Alvarenga ’2
 8</strong>\, English and Educational Studies\; <strong>Shea Kozel ’28</
 strong>\, Political Science and International Relations\; <strong>Kumail 
 Akram ’29\;</strong> and<strong> James Russ ’29</strong>\, as they t
 alk more about the program\, their experience\, and the application proces
 s.\n\nLunch will be provided by Colorado College from the <a href="https:
 //thehideawaynorthfield.com/food-menu">Hideaway</a> <i>(Downtown menu)</i
 >. Register to attend\, and add your food preference to this <a href="htt
 ps://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/17nV9PZOBLXEGqK--NMpxjTcxdT9M7_6O_1NqN
 DnxDQ4/edit?usp=sharing">sheet</a>!\n\n</div>\n\nView this event on the Ca
 rleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut2C
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
