SUMMARY:Dream of the Red Chamber and the Female Readers' Responsive Poetry
  in the Nineteenth Century -  Ann Waltner\, Professor of History\, Univers
 ity of Minnesota
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:LDC 104
DESCRIPTION:The Dr. Walter H. Judd Lectureship in Asian Studies fall talk 
 is presented by Ann Waltner\, Professor of History\, University of Minneso
 ta\, titled "<em>Dream of the Red Chamber and the Female Readers' Responsi
 ve Poetry in the Nineteenth Century."</em>\n\nThe Dream of the Red Chamber
  (or The Story of the Stone) stands as one of China’s Four Great Classic
 al Novels. Long before its official publication in 1791\, it captured the 
 imagination of readers—and sparked a rich tradition of literary commenta
 ry. Join us for a talk exploring this monumental work and the vibrant poet
 ry written by young female readers who engaged with it throughout the 19th
  century.\n\nThis event is sponsored by The Dr. Walter H. Judd Lectureship
  in Asian Studies and organized by the Department of Asian Languages &amp\
 ; Literatures.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps:
 //www.carleton.edu/_c/uuh4
ORGANIZER;CN="Asian Languages & Literatures Events":mailto:skcpmiavor6qol1
 6m8vnq9cod0@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260907T162519
END:VEVENT
