SUMMARY:The Hurt Locker with Sound Designer\, Paul Ottosson
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz Cinema
DESCRIPTION:Watch <strong>The Hurt Locker</strong>\, the winner of the 200
 9 Academy Award for Best Picture followed by a Q&amp\;A with Academy Award
  winning sound designer\, Paul Ottosson.\n<p class="cvGsUA block-font-kern
 ing-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off block-fon
 t-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-center" style="text-align: left"><s
 pan class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature
 -calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none"><strong>The Hurt L
 ocker</strong> is a 2008 American war film directed by Kathryn Bigelow and
  written by Mark Boal. It stars Jeremy Renner\, Anthony Mackie\, Brian Ger
 aghty\, Christian Cmargo\, Ralph Fiennes\, David Morse\, and Guy Pearce. I
 t follows an Iraq War bomb disposal team who are targeted by insurgents an
 d shows their psychological reactions to the stress of combat. Boal drew o
 n his experience during embedded accesss to write the screenplay. it was h
 ominated for nine Academy Awards and won six\, becoming the first film dir
 ected by a woman to win Best Picture.</span></p>\n<p class="cvGsUA block-f
 ont-kerning-none block-font-feature-liga-off block-font-feature-clig-off b
 lock-font-feature-calt-off direction-ltr align-center" style="text-align: 
 left"><span class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font
 -feature-calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Paul Ottos
 son is a Swedish sound designer. He is the recipient of numerous accolades
 \, including three Academy Awards\, two for his work on <strong>The Hurt L
 ocker</strong>.</span></p>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College webs
 ite:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuiD
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton Arts Calendar":mailto:m3mgdme4j7u3ame5pt83faap1g@gr
 oup.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260917T185416
END:VEVENT
