SUMMARY:Field Notes Artist Talk #1
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Perlman Teaching Museum
DESCRIPTION:<em>Field Notes</em> presents new work by Carleton studio art 
 faculty in response to the Carleton College Cowling Arboretum’s landscap
 es\, histories\, and ecological significance. It marks the 100th anniversa
 ry of the Arboretum\, an 800-acre living laboratory of prairie\, forest\, 
 and river habitats that has shaped teaching\, research\, and life on campu
 s since the 1920s.\n\nThe accompanying events program will include talks b
 y participating studio art faculty\, offering insight into their creative 
 processes.\n\nAt the end of each faculty artist talk\, one lucky attendee 
 will be raffled a <a href="https://fieldnotesbrand.com/products/expedition
 ">Field Notes Expedition waterproof notebook</a>\, a perfect accompaniment
  to your adventures in the Arb and beyond!\n\n<strong>Today's featured spe
 akers: Eleanor Jensen and Stephen Mohring</strong>\n\nView this event on t
 he Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uujm
