SUMMARY:Joy Luck Trio
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Kracum Performance Hall
DESCRIPTION:<span data-sheets-root="1">Joy Luck Trio—the world’s first
  pipa\, erhu\, and piano ensemble—invites audiences into a sound world a
 t once ancient and new.Gao Hong (pipa)\, Karen Han (erhu)\, and Donna Weng
  Friedman (piano) reimagine Western masterpieces through improvisation and
  bring Chinese folktales\, memories\, and landscapes to life in new works 
 by Gao Hong. In their hands\, the voices of East and West meet with extrao
 rdinary beauty and emotional depth—music that has moved audience members
  to tears. Hailed by <em>Crushing Classical</em> as “a new supergroup\,
 ” Joy Luck Trio will release its first recording on Naxos World in Febru
 ary 2027\, ahead of Lunar New Year. As one reviewer wrote\, “It made me 
 hear music in a way I never had before.”</span>\n\nView this event on th
 e Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuaW
ORGANIZER;CN="Music Department":mailto:4hvg0t6h02sui82j4vqmmqbeag@group.ca
 lendar.google.com
