SUMMARY:Experiencing Spain: Ecology\, Economy\, and Socio-Political Transi
 tions Info Session
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Virtual Meeting
DESCRIPTION:This interdisciplinary and civically engaged program is perfec
 t for adventurous travelers eager to live in Spain and immerse themselves 
 in the country’s rich political\, social\, historical\, economic\, and c
 ultural fabric—all while mastering the language.\n\nMost students partic
 ipating in the program are non-majors in their sophomore and junior years.
  Applicants must have completed SPAN 205\, equivalent or above by spring t
 erm 2025. Given the competitive nature of the program\, student selection 
 also rests on a combination of factors\, such as performance during the in
 terview\, GPA\, letters of recommendation\, application form\, language pr
 oficiency\, and group dynamics.\n\nEvent Details:\nhttps://www.carleton.ed
 u/ocs/madrid/\n\nConnect to Virtual Event:\nhttps://meet.google.com/qky-vx
 mz-deo?authuser=0\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhtt
 ps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut8o
ORGANIZER;CN="Off Campus Studies":mailto:4iqiub2cjhnjgpqu2joiv600f8@group.
 calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260622T180705
