SUMMARY:Interconnected and Othered: Unpacking Antisemitism and Anti-Muslim
  Bias on Campus and Beyond
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:<span style="font-weight: 400">Come join Chaplains Fatima Bash
 arat and Michaela Brown as they explore how anti-Muslim bias and antisemit
 ism impact both our campus community and our wider world. Together\, we'll
  dive into misconceptions about religious identity and practice\, historic
 al contexts for discrimination and bias\, the lived experience of students
 \, and how Carleton can make campus a safe and welcoming place for all. A 
 complementary catered dinner will be served\, courtesy of the Division of 
 Inclusion\, Equity\, and Community. All are welcome!</span>\n\nThis event 
 forms part of IDE Community Education.\n\n<a href="https://forms.gle/4gMWM
 Lgk7BHiVJrg6">Register Here</a>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College
