SUMMARY:Arboretum Volunteer Work Event
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Arboretum Office\, 710 Three Oaks Drive\, Northfield\, MN
DESCRIPTION:Join us to improve the prairies of the Arboretum by removing a
 spen and other invading brush. Historically our prairies were primarily tr
 eeless\, providing important habitat for birds\, insects and other animals
  that depend on this declining resource.  At this work event we will cut 
 small stems and carefully treat the cut stem with herbicide. Volunteers ca
 n choose what activity suits them best. We  require participants at this 
 event to be 18 years of age. We suggest long pants\, closed toe shoes and 
 socks and your own water bottle.\n\nView this event on the Carleton Colleg
 e website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuiz
ORGANIZER;CN="Cowling Arboretum":mailto:arsa1npokgd6u28r3pibqv644s@group.c
 alendar.google.com
