SUMMARY:Strategies for Coping with Grief\, Trauma &amp\; Beyond
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://click.sfmail.healthadvocate.com/?qs=ABB7InYiO
 jEsImQiOjQ5NjB9AAcAAAAABO8Vw4ZUA-rVxdIgkQsa61rWWdWu_MyFRj4Dvyxu_y5Ox3qBTBL
 FqreCE8_pShu0Vy2e010dAzVqx6UNyGMBl-RlO0aDTw">Register here</a> for this fr
 ee webinar offered through our Employee Assistance Program (EAP)\, Health 
 Advocate.\n\nNews and social media are full of negative\, disturbing\, and
  tragic events that can have an impact on our well-being and productivity.
  Learning how to cope with upsetting events can help us stay grounded\, be
  engaged at work\, and reduce the impact of information overload.\n\nJoin 
 us for a webinar to explore strategies for managing difficult news\, navig
 ating sensitive conversations with coworkers\, and protecting your well-be
 ing in challenging times.\n\nTopics to be covered:\n<ul>\n 	<li>Understand
 ing information overload</li>\n 	<li>Managing exposure to negative news</l
 i>\n 	<li>Coping during times of uncertainty</li>\n</ul>\nPresenter: Karen
  Beaudoin\, MSW\, EAP Program Manager &amp\; Senior Trainer\, Health Advoc
 ate\n\nEvent Details:\nhttps://click.sfmail.healthadvocate.com/?qs=ABB7InY
 iOjEsImQiOjQ5NjB9AAcAAAAABO8Vw4ZUA-rVxdIgkQsa61rWWdWu_MyFRj4Dvyxu_y5Ox3qBT
 BLFqreCE8_pShu0Vy2e010dAzVqx6UNyGMBl-RlO0aDTw\n\nView this event on the Ca
 rleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut2j
ORGANIZER;CN="Human Resources":mailto:b15mhdjetki0bmiaka260hdoh0@group.cal
 endar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T205414
END:VEVENT
