 Meditation</a> in partnership with The Office of Health Promotion led by <
 a href="https://www.marcanderson.org/bio">Marc Anderson</a>.\n\nAn immersi
 ve experience in which the listener is “bathed” in waves of soft tones
 \, shifting textures and gentle rhythms. Combining the sounds of crystal s
 inging bowls\, gongs\, hand drums and subtle drones Marc creates a rich an
 d deeply therapeutic experience. His extensive background as a musician an
 d meditation teacher\, supported by years of studying trance related music
 /healing traditions\, allows him to create unique\, powerful\, well-crafte
 d sessions that restore\, relax and transform.\n\nMarc Anderson is a Twin 
 Cities based musician\, composer\, Zen priest and poet. He has studied\, p
 erformed and recorded music all over the world with hundreds of great arti
 sts including\; Angelique Kidjo\, Robert Fripp\, Steve Tibbetts\, Don Cher
 ry\, Max Roach and Taj Mahal. He founded and directs the M2 Foundation whi
 ch advocates for a more mindful and compassionate world. And\, he is on st
 aff in the Center for Religious and Spiritual Life at Macalester College.\
 n\nDinner provided following the meditation.\n\nAll are welcome and invite
 d to bring a pillow and/or blanket to the event!\n\nView this event on the
  Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/utYu
ORGANIZER;CN="Chaplain's Office":mailto:gc0r4cojm5g3aensafau0dppd8@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260605T195527
END:VEVENT
