SUMMARY:Quaker Voluntary Service Tabling at Sayles
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:<a href="https://apps.carleton.edu/map/sayles/">Sayles Tables</a>
DESCRIPTION:<img class="" src="https://d31kydh6n6r5j5.cloudfront.net/uploa
 ds/sites/676/2021/06/1657573.jpg" alt="Quaker Voluntary Service" width="26
 6" height="108" data-name="image" />\n<div class="property-box">\n<div cla
 ss="text-heavy sanitized-html-container">\n\n<strong>Live your values whil
 e gaining valuable job skills and living in a community! </strong>\n<div>
 \n<div>\n\n<strong><a href="https://quakervoluntaryservice.org/" target="_
 blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.
 com/url?q=https://quakervoluntaryservice.org/&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1
 787064447146000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3QRf3iLXmMbjWiK9lpyMfM">Quaker Voluntary Se
 rvice</a></strong> (QVS) is an experiment at the intersection of transfor
 mational spirituality and activism\, an 11-month Fellowship program for yo
 ung adults aged 21-30. Check out all of their openings via <a href="https
 ://carleton.joinhandshake.com/edu/employers/57369/jobs?page=1&amp\;per_pag
 e=25&amp\;sort_direction=desc&amp\;sort_column=expiration_date&amp\;status
 Toggle=active&amp\;category=UniversityPostings&amp\;employers=57369" targe
 t="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url
 ?q=https://carleton.joinhandshake.com/edu/employers/57369/jobs?page%3D1%26
 per_page%3D25%26sort_direction%3Ddesc%26sort_column%3Dexpiration_date%26st
 atusToggle%3Dactive%26category%3DUniversityPostings%26employers%3D57369&am
 p\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1787064447146000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2fBLFSweZkZNFogMa
 ky_4y">Handshake</a>.\n\nParticipants engage in social justice work\, live
  in an intentional community\, and explore Quaker practices around decisio
 n-making\, sustainability\, discernment\, and simplicity.\n\nParticipating
  Fellows receive room\, board\, transportation\, a monthly stipend\, and s
 upport of QVS staff and local meeting members among many other benefits. Q
 VS currently has houses in Minneapolis\, Boston\, Philadelphia\, and Portl
 and\, OR.\n\nQVS Recruiting Manager\, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/i
 n/ruth-cutcher/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="http
 s://www.google.com/url?q=https://www.linkedin.com/in/ruth-cutcher/&amp\;so
 urce=gmail&amp\;ust=1787064447146000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2L6c0QpwcugQ35iQUEdE5E
 ">Ruth Cutcher</a>\, will be on-campus to answer your questions and discus
 s how a QVS year could fit into your post-grad options by launching your c
 areer in the social justice non-profit sector.\n\n</div>\n</div>\n<div><a 
 href="https://quakervoluntaryservice.org/about-us/staff/">Ray Hommeier</a>
 \, the Minneapolis/St. Paul Coordinator\, manages all aspects of a year-lo
 ng service Fellowship\, including establishing partnerships with local jus
 tice-oriented organizations and recruiting Fellows. During the Fellowship 
 year\, Ray supports the material and spiritual health of Fellows by facili
 tating group processing and individual check-ins.</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\
 nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.ed
 u/_c/ut4W
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
