SUMMARY:Isla Internships Abroad - Intern in Armenia\, Bulgaria\, Greece\, 
 Kosovo\, India\, North Macedonia\, or Spain
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:<a href="https://carleton.edu/map/sayles/">Sayles 253</a>\; For m
 ore information or to register\, see <a href="https://carleton.joinhandsha
 ke.com/events/2008686/share_preview/">Handshake</a>
DESCRIPTION:<img src="https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploads/sites/676/2024/10/d
 ownload-1.png" alt="Isla Internships Abroad Logo" data-name="image" />\n\n
 <a href="https://www.isla-serve.org/"><strong>Isla Internships Abroad</str
 ong></a> (Isla) is a U.S.-based organization founded by Returned Peace Co
 rps Volunteers\, with a mission of bringing a “mini Peace Corps experien
 ce” to students. Isla partners with universities to place students in gl
 obal development internships customized to match their specific skills and
  interests. Isla helps create a truly immersive and “all-inclusive” in
 ternational experience\, where professional\, academic\, cultural\, and so
 cial opportunities are all a part of the experience.\n\nIsla internships a
 re based on the United Nations Sustainable Development Goals and are commu
 nity-based initiatives. Isla believes local people and organizations shoul
 d guide development in their communities. Isla participants are partners a
 nd catalysts in making a positive impact alongside Isla's local and intern
 ational host organizations and communities.\n\nIsla works out all of the l
 ogistics for interns- from housing\, airport pick-up\, insurance\, and mor
 e! Each of the locations has a 24/7 support team to assist interns through
 out their experience!\n\nIf you are seeking international work experience 
 in a global development context\, Isla is for you! Hear more about Isla In
 ternships and the opportunity to intern in Armenia\, Bulgaria\, Greece\, K
 osovo\, India\, North Macedonia\, or Spain\, from previous interns\, <a h
 ref="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kelly-santillan-villegas-aa4185262/"><str
 ong>Kelly Santillan Villegas ’27</strong></a>\, <a href="https://www.li
 nkedin.com/in/adria-major-448211273/"><strong>Adria Major ’27</strong></
 a>\, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lucia-caputo-36155228a/"><stron
 g>Lucia Caputo ’27</strong></a>\, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/
 isaac-hoffman-2a4858324/"><strong>Isaac Hoffman ’28</strong></a>\, and E
 xecutive Director\, <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/leila-ali-071393
 104/"><strong>Leila Ali</strong></a>.\n\nThere are currently <a href="htt
 ps://carleton.joinhandshake.com/edu/employers/865446/jobs?statusToggle=act
 ive&amp\;category=UniversityPostings&amp\;employers=865446&amp\;sort_colum
 n=job.name.case_insensitive_sorting&amp\;sort_direction=asc&amp\;page=1&am
 p\;per_page=100"><strong>34 opportunities</strong></a> in every career se
 ctor listed on Handshake for next summer. See the sampling below:\n\n<stro
 ng>Sectors/ Career Fields:</strong>\n<ul>\n 	<li>Agriculture &amp\; Permac
 ulture</li>\n 	<li>Arts\, Culture &amp\; Social Impact</li>\n 	<li>Busines
 s\, IT &amp\; Entrepreneurship</li>\n 	<li>Democracy &amp\; Governance</li
 >\n 	<li>Education</li>\n 	<li>Engineering</li>\n 	<li>Environmental Susta
 inability</li>\n 	<li>Global Health &amp\; Medicine</li>\n 	<li>Human Righ
 ts\, Social Justice &amp\; Law</li>\n 	<li>Social Work</li>\n 	<li>Wildlif
 e Conservation</li>\n 	<li>Youth &amp\; Sports</li>\n</ul>\nCome check it 
 out and ask any questions you may have!\n\nLunch will be provided. Please 
 register!\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www
 .carleton.edu/_c/ut9o
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260831T212921
END:VEVENT
