SUMMARY:Queer Mental Health Collective: The Intersections of Queerness and
  Disability
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Sayles 251
DESCRIPTION:Join Queer Mental Health Collective as we discuss  Intersectio
 ns of Queerness and Disability.\n\nFood from Tin Tea provided (limited). N
 o registration required.\n\nThe Queer Mental Health Collective at Carleton
  College is a safe space for LGBTQIA+ students to form community through c
 onversation and actively supporting one another’s mental health and well
 being. We believe shared spaces can be healing for those living with the e
 ffects of queer/transphobia and other social injustices at individual\, co
 mmunity and systemic levels.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College we
 bsite:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uujM
ORGANIZER;CN="Queer Mental Health Collective":mailto:8ee0d590a41978e92376f
 bf4f307cfa338785be6221d5ffa3e9677a72f6be10e@group.calendar.google.com
