SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T045925
DTSTART:20261022T150000
DTEND:20261022T160000
SUMMARY:Carl Talks—Wars\, violence\, and madness: Lessons of trauma and 
 healing from global fieldwork with Anushka Patel '12
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:virtual
DESCRIPTION:<h3 style="text-align: center">Carl Talks\n<em><b>\n</b></em><
 i>Wars\, violence\, and madness:\nLessons of trauma and healing from globa
 l fieldwork\n</i>with Anushka Patel '12</h3>\n<h4 style="text-align: cente
 r">Thursday\, October 22\, 2026\n3 p.m. Central Time\nvia Zoom</h4>\n<div>
 <img class="alignright" src="https://cdn.carleton.edu/uploads/sites/736/20
 26/09/Professional_pic-copy-e1788899283242.png" alt="" width="270" height=
 "273" data-name="image" />Dr. Anushka R. Patel is an Assistant Professor a
 t Harvard Medical School. She is a trauma-focused clinical psychologist sp
 ecializing in assessing and treating trauma-related problems with a cultur
 al lens in low-resource settings. Dr. Patel concentrates on survivors of g
 ender-based and interpersonal violence\, using community-based participato
 ry approaches in her work. Her focus is to create scalable models of traum
 a-informed care in low-resource settings worldwide. Her program of researc
 h has been continuously funded by NIH since 2021\, and her work has been c
 ited in <i>Al Jazeera </i>and<i> New York Times</i>. Dr. Patel graduated
  from Carleton in 2012 having majored in psychology and cross-cultural stu
 dies.\n\n</div>\n<div>Dr. Patel’s talk will focus on the impact of inter
 personal trauma worldwide. She will connect research on treatment\, publi
 c health\, and her own lessons from her fieldwork in low-resource settings
 .</div>\n<strong>Register</strong> <strong>by Wednesday\, October 21 </str
 ong>to participate in this Zoom event.\n\n<strong>Cost:</strong> None.\n\n
 Unable to join our live event? No problem — we will post a recording of 
 the event on our <a href="https://www.carleton.edu/alumni/news/recordings/
 "><strong>Alumni Events Recordings</strong></a> page.\n\n<strong>Question
 s?</strong> Contact Alumni Relations via <a href="mailto:alumni-office@car
 leton.edu?subject=Carleton%20event%20question"><strong>email</strong></a> 
 or 800-729-2586.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttp
 s://www.carleton.edu/_c/uubf
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton’s Regional Carls Program":mailto:r7km2dafnqvrponn
 mp387i2vgg@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260908T202311
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
