SUMMARY:Harvard Divinity School Information Session
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:<a href="https://apps.carleton.edu/map/agh/">Alumni Guest House</
 a>\; For more information or to register\, see <a href="https://carleton.j
 oinhandshake.com/edu/events/1982155/">Handshake</a>
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://hds.harvard.edu/"><img src="https://d31kydh6n
 6r5j5.cloudfront.net/uploads/sites/676/2021/06/1311761.jpg" alt="Harvard D
 ivinity School" data-name="image" /></a>\n\n<a href="https://www.hds.harva
 rd.edu/people/margaret-okada-scheck">Margaret Okada-Scheck</a>\, Associate
  Director of Admissions at <a href="https://hds.harvard.edu/" target="_bla
 nk" rel="noopener">Harvard Divinity School\,</a> will be holding a virtual
  information session to talk about HDS's <a href="https://hds.harvard.edu/
 academics" target="_blank" rel="noopener">graduate programs</a>. Students 
 will all gather in person\, and lunch will be provided.\n\nHDS graduates e
 ngage in a wide variety of professions. They continue in academic careers 
 and go on to educate future scholars and teachers of religion and theology
 \; they become ministers and leaders in their own religious traditions\; t
 hey work in public service and with governmental\, nongovernmental\, and s
 ocial organizations\, in nonprofits and in business\, in the arts\, in hea
 lth care\, and in other professions.\n\n<strong>Interesting fact:\n</stron
 g>For many years now\, Carleton has dominated HDS' alma mater-- by far! So
  there's quite a community of Carls in the Boston area. And it isn't just 
 for Christians or people headed into parish ministry--Harvard has worked h
 ard to be relevant for people of all religious backgrounds and headed into
  many fields (diplomacy\, social service\, and social change work\, academ
 ia\, medicine\, and hospital and college chaplaincy\, in addition to more 
 pastoral ministries).\n\n<strong>Fun facts:</strong>\nCarleton's Chaplain\
 , <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/schuyler-vogel-51a357a/">Schuyler V
 ogel ’07</a>\, is a Harvard Divinity graduate. Carleton faculty members\
 , <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristin-bloomer-539b0925/">Kristin 
 Bloomer</a> and <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/lori-pearson-b522a81/
 ">Lori Pearson</a>\, were both visiting professors at Harvard. Lori is a g
 raduate of the institution.<span aria-hidden="true"> Lori is a graduate o
 f the institution.</span>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College websi
 te:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut2o
ORGANIZER;CN="Career Center Events":mailto:e6n22m53s4lq205dsr03tqqlf4@grou
 p.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260729T182109
END:VEVENT
