SUMMARY:Interfaith Social Action (IFSA)
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Chapel Lounge
DESCRIPTION:Interfaith Social Action meets weekly to engage issues that in
 tersect with faith and social justice. We work across faith traditions to 
 take action on challenges that affect both Carleton\, the Northfield commu
 nity\, state\, national\, and even global communities. We practice our val
 ues through meaningful dialogue\, learning\, advocacy\, community service\
 , and activism. Most recently IFSA has responded to transportation deficie
 ncies and food insecurity on campus\, and the needs of immigrant neighbors
  during Operation Metro Surge. We welcome anyone to join us at any point d
 uring the year\, whether you are a person of faith\, or a person of good c
 onscience who wants to make a difference.\n\nView this event on the Carlet
 on College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/roPZ
ORGANIZER;CN="Chaplain's Office":mailto:gc0r4cojm5g3aensafau0dppd8@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260713T194034
