SUMMARY:What Matters to Me and Why: Chielo Eze
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz 236
DESCRIPTION:Chielo Eze is Professor of Africana Studies at Carleton Colleg
 e and a Research Associate at Nelson Mandela University in South Africa. P
 rior to joining Carleton\, he served as the Bernard J. Brommel Distinguish
 ed Research Professor at Northeastern Illinois University in Chicago and a
 s Extraordinary Professor of English at Stellenbosch University in South A
 frica. In addition to publishing more than thirty articles in leading peer
 -reviewed journals\, he is the author of Race\, Decolonization\, and Globa
 l Citizenship in South Africa (University of Rochester Press\, 2018) and J
 ustice and Human Rights in the African Imagination: We\, Too\, Are Humans 
 (Routledge\, 2021). His most recent book\, Zora Neale Hurston\nand the Leg
 acy of Black Feminism: Desire as Power\, was published by Bloomsbury in Ja
 nuary 2025.\n\n<a href="https://www.carleton.edu/chaplain/resources-and-re
 flections/reflections-what-matters-to-me-and-why/">What Matters to Me and 
 Why?</a> is a continuing series of faculty and staff talks on life\, work\
 , and meaning. Every term\, staff/faculty members are invited to explore t
 he question: what matters to you and why?\n\nThese conversations are a won
 derful opportunity for students\, faculty\, and staff to come to know the 
 people at Carleton in a deeper\, more personal way. Lunch is provided.\n\n
 If you would like to nominate a speaker\, please email our College Chaplai
 n\, Schuyler Vogel\, at svogel@carleton.edu. We strive to represent the fu
 ll diversity of staff and faculty on campus and welcome nominations regard
 less of role or longevity. All members of the Carleton community have wisd
 om to share.\n\nThe series is cosponsored with EthIC.\n\nLunch is provided
 .\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleto
 n.edu/_c/ut1f
ORGANIZER;CN="Chaplain's Office":mailto:gc0r4cojm5g3aensafau0dppd8@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260729T182521
END:VEVENT
