SUMMARY:Convocation with Lilliana Hall Mason
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Skinner Memorial Chapel
DESCRIPTION:Lilliana Mason is an SNF Agora Institute Professor of Politica
 l Science. She is the author of <a href="https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/b
 ooks/book/chicago/U/bo27527354.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-s
 aferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://press.uchicago.edu/uc
 p/books/book/chicago/U/bo27527354.html&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=17871626
 16298000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw18DkYmPGnykoOk2XNjfKep"><i>Uncivil Agreement: How 
 Politics Became Our Identity</i></a> and co-author\, with Nathan P. Kalmo
 e\, of <a href="https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/R/bo163
 195227.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://
 www.google.com/url?q=https://press.uchicago.edu/ucp/books/book/chicago/R/b
 o163195227.html&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1787162616298000&amp\;usg=AOvVa
 w3AbVzoLsalnVU2LBSRX7qB"><i>Radical American Partisanship: Mapping Violent
  Hostility\, Its Causes\, and the Consequences for Democracy</i></a><i>. 
 </i>She received her PhD in political psychology from Stony Brook Universi
 ty and her BA in politics from Princeton University. Her research on parti
 san identity\, social sorting\, and political violence has been published 
 in journals such as <i>American Political Science Review</i>\, <i>Americ
 an Journal of Political Science</i>\, and <i>Journal of Politics</i>\, an
 d featured in media outlets including <i>the</i> <i>New York Times</i>\,
  <i>the Washington Post</i>\, <i>CNN</i>\, and <i>National Public Radio
 </i>. Her work has been supported by the National Science Foundation\, the
  Facebook Research Integrity Group\, the Democracy Fund\, and the Andrew C
 arnegie Foundation (formerly Carnegie Corporation of New York).\n\nHer pre
 sentation is called A New Look at Polarization: The American Divide Over P
 luralism.\n\nThis convocation is also presented as a virtual webinar. <a 
 href="https://carleton.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_FwddI0MdR3m83cCRWRIA2Q"
 >Please register in advance if you would like to attend via Zoom.</a> Afte
 r registering\, you will receive a confirmation email containing informati
 on about joining the webinar.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College w
 ebsite:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut5O
ORGANIZER;CN="Convocations":mailto:g8h62604doarbi9ihcipmnhd04@group.calend
 ar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260806T162704
END:VEVENT
