SUMMARY:A Conversation with Hernán Díaz\, Winner of the 2023 Pulitzer Pr
 ize for Fiction: His Work and His Place in American Literature
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Olin 149
DESCRIPTION:Across these two remarkably different novels\, Díaz returns t
 o some of the foundational myths of American culture—the frontier\, the 
 self-made individual\, money\, power\, and the creation of enormous wealth
 —while radically reinventing the literary forms through which those myth
 s have traditionally been told. <i>In the Distance</i> reimagines the We
 stern from the perspective of a lost immigrant moving against the great we
 stward migration\; <i>Trust</i> takes apart the novel of wealth and fina
 nce by telling the same story through four competing narratives. In both\,
  Díaz inhabits recognizable American genres only to estrange them from wi
 thin\, asking who gets to tell the stories through which America imagines 
 itself.\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.c
 arleton.edu/_c/uubo
ORGANIZER;CN="Spanish":mailto:h918ecruebjd3u5pdqud3gf3sk@group.calendar.go
 ogle.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260909T140926
END:VEVENT
