SUMMARY:Indigenous Engagement: Our Presence on Dakota Land
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:AGH 114
DESCRIPTION:<span style="font-weight: 400">The region in which Carleton is
  located has been regarded by Dakota as homelands for time immemorial. Joi
 n Indigenous Communities Liaison\, Marcy Averill\, to explore how we can m
 ove beyond acknowledgement of our position within these lands into allyshi
 p and partnership. In this workshop\, we will challenge ourselves to consi
 der ethical and reciprocal engagement practices and partnerships as define
 d by Dakota leaders. Historical context will be examined\, mapped to curre
 nt challenges\, and connected to expanding initiatives in Indigenous Engag
 ement at Carleton.</span>\n\nThis event forms part of IDE Community Educat
 ion.\n\n<a href="https://www.myworkday.com/carleton/learning/course/38f9a9
 07271b1001fe6ed9dc9ed00000?type=9882927d138b100019b6a2df1a46018b">Register
  on Workday</a>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps
 ://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut8S
ORGANIZER;CN="Division of Inclusion, Equity, and Community":mailto:l60qmlb
 93d9qlrf78jk9i21bms@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260828T185939
END:VEVENT
