SUMMARY:Arboretum Centennial Speaker Series: The Six Lives of the Cowling 
 Arboretum with Ingrid Case '90 and Nat Case '88
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz Cinema
DESCRIPTION:"<span id="m_-39606867232420410gmail-docs-internal-guid-ef7a14
 63-7fff-b7f9-215e-841f5f9a1d10">When we walk into a 'natural'  area\, it 
 can feel like we're entering an eternal space. This can deceive. The area 
 that is now Carleton College's Arb has changed and changed again over its 
 human history\, and how people have regarded the land has changed\, too. W
 e'll look at the Arboretum as Dakota land\; as small farms\; in its first 
 era as Carleton's Arboretum and Farm\; in its role as a rougher\, unchaper
 oned space in the turbulent 1960s\; and in its newest transformation over 
 the last 50 years into a treasured\, organized part of the Carleton projec
 t.</span>"\n\nPlease join us for the second presentation of the Arboretum 
 Centennial Speaker Series\, <em>The Six Lives of the Cowling Arboretum</em
 > with Ingrid Case '90 and Nat Case ('88)\, co-authors of the recently pub
 lished book\, <a href="https://bridge.primo.exlibrisgroup.com/permalink/01
 BRC_INST/1c09093/alma991018976873802971">Into the Arb : a history of the C
 owling Arboretum at Carleton College</a>.\n\nView this event on the Carlet
 on College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut6v
ORGANIZER;CN="Cowling Arboretum":mailto:arsa1npokgd6u28r3pibqv644s@group.c
 alendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260813T193922
END:VEVENT
