TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Weitz 236
DESCRIPTION:<p class="p1"><strong>STUDENT USE OF ASSISTIVE TECHNOLOGY</str
 ong></p>\n<p class="p1">What accessibility tools are already built into th
 e devices Carleton students carry every day? This session from Academic Te
 chnology\, the Office of Accessibility Resources\, and Assistive Technolog
 ists covers built-in features - including screen readers\, audio text\, di
 ctation\, and focus tools\, third-party apps\, and campus support\, with e
 arly survey findings about current student usage where available.</p>\n<p 
 class="p1">*This event counts towards IDE Community Education.</p>\n<p cla
 ss="p1">Don Vosburg\, Academic Technologist of Learning Innovation\nSam Th
 ayer\, Director\, Office of Accessibility Resources</p>\n\nView this event
  on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uufL
