SUMMARY:Staying Healthy and Happy While Working from Home
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
DESCRIPTION:In this session\, we will discuss topics including five tips f
 or adjusting to working from home\, managing time and setting boundaries\,
  staying visible and connected when working from home\, and working from h
 ome with children. We will discuss best practices and practical advice to 
 help you stay connected. We will discuss starting your day off right\, cre
 ating a dedicated workspace\, creating a schedule\, setting boundaries\, r
 ule-setting for children\, children’s activities\, communication expecta
 tions\, and much more!\n\nThis webinar will be presented by Susan Ferraro\
 , PMHNP\, R.N.\, M.S.\, a Health Advocate EAP-affiliated facilitator.\n\nS
 taff and faculty must <a href="https://www.myworkday.com/carleton/learning
 /course/74d6bfb6833d1000c7d86374d0180000?type=9882927d138b100019b6a2df1a46
 018b">register for this webinar</a> through Workday. Upon enrolling\, the 
 Zoom link will be available through Workday Learning and the calendar invi
 te that you will receive from Workday.\n\nView this event on the Carleton 
 College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut9L
ORGANIZER;CN="Human Resources":mailto:b15mhdjetki0bmiaka260hdoh0@group.cal
 endar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260811T144955
END:VEVENT
