SUMMARY:Computation\, Past and Present\, in England Info Session
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Leighton 236
DESCRIPTION:This program explores the history of computing\, with a partic
 ular focus on two eras during which there was a particularly strong Britis
 h role: the mid-1800s\, when the first programmable devices were being des
 igned (at the level of blueprints\, not actual physical devices)\, and the
  mid-1900s\, when the first physical programmable computers were built as 
 part of the Allied efforts in World War II.\n\nEvent Details:\nhttps://www
 .carleton.edu/ocs/computing\n\nView this event on the Carleton College web
 site:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/uuhH
ORGANIZER;CN="Off Campus Studies":mailto:4iqiub2cjhnjgpqu2joiv600f8@group.
 calendar.google.com
