SUMMARY:The Disharmony Blueprint:  A Two-Part Series on Intercultural Comm
 unication and Relationship Repair Part Two
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:AGH 114
DESCRIPTION:<span style="font-weight: 400">This two-part series will suppo
 rt Carleton faculty and staff in building practical skills for navigating 
 intercultural communication\, conflict\, and relationship repair\, grounde
 d in restorative justice practices and two complementary theoretical frame
 works: Kathryn Sorrells' model of intercultural praxis and Bernard Mayer's
  dynamics-of-conflict model. </span>\n\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Th
 is event is part of IDE Community Education</span>\n\n<a href="https://www
 .myworkday.com/carleton/learning/course/38f9a907271b1001efb305ff4cbb0000?t
 ype=9882927d138b100019b6a2df1a46018b">Register on Workday</a>\n\nFacilitat
 ed by: <a href="https://www.thetainacollective.com/">Dr. Aida Martinez-Fre
 eman</a> and Michelle Sylvester\n\nView this event on the Carleton College
  website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut8Q
ORGANIZER;CN="Division of Inclusion, Equity, and Community":mailto:l60qmlb
 93d9qlrf78jk9i21bms@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260828T150032
END:VEVENT
