SUMMARY:What Is a Community Circle? Come Find Out ...
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:AGH Library
DESCRIPTION:<span style="font-weight: 400">If you’ve never participated 
 in a Circle before\, this session is for you! A Community Building Circle 
 is simply a structured way to have a conversation where everyone has an eq
 ual chance to speak and listen—without interruption or crosstalk. The ai
 m of the circle is to build community.</span>\n\n<span style="font-weight:
  400">We’re hosting an informal gathering for faculty and staff to try o
 ut the format together. Whether you're interested in how Circles work for 
 campus life or just want a quiet space to connect with colleagues outside 
 your department\, all are welcome. Just bring yourself and your curiosity!
 </span>\n\n<b>What it IS:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> A casual spac
 e to share stories\, listen to colleagues\, and pause. </span>\n\n<b>What
  it ISN'T:</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> Group therapy\, conflict res
 olution\, or a heavy training session.  </span>\n\n<a href="https://docs
 .google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdULf6H_ZXOHABjIcikaOsLAbbiX4emshY_Ws3VaRqMMA
 DhcQ/viewform?usp=header"><span style="font-weight: 400">Sign Up Here - Go
 ogle Form</span></a>\n\n<span style="font-weight: 400">Time: Noon to 1 pm\
 , including lunch in the AGH Library</span>\n\nFacilitated by: Christine H
 amp and Travis Blomberg\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website
 :\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut3J
ORGANIZER;CN="Division of Inclusion, Equity, and Community":mailto:l60qmlb
 93d9qlrf78jk9i21bms@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260814T152700
END:VEVENT
