SUMMARY:Beyond the Chapel: Tour of Carleton's Sacred Sites
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:TBD
DESCRIPTION:<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400">Joi
 n College <a href="svogel@carleton.edu">Chaplain Schuyler Vogel</a> for a 
 tour of Carleton sacred sites beyond Skinner Memorial Chapel. We'll explor
 e spaces including the Japanese Garden\, Indigenous Sacred Space\, Druid C
 ircle\, Student Memorial\, and the Stewsie Island Labyrinth. Come learn ab
 out the history of these spaces\, how they are used today\, and how they o
 ffer our community grounding\, inspiration\, and connection. </span>\n\n<
 span style="font-weight: 400">This event forms part of the IDE Community E
 ducation. Please advise <a href="mailto:msylvester@carleton.edu">msylveste
 r@carleton.edu</a> of any accommodations.</span>\n\n<a href="https://www.m
 yworkday.com/carleton/learning/course/153a841b28d31001f1f64e3117e50000?typ
 e=9882927d138b100019b6a2df1a46018b"><span style="font-weight: 400">Registe
 r through Workday</span></a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n\nView this 
 event on the Carleton College website:\nhttps://www.carleton.edu/_c/ut3L
ORGANIZER;CN="Division of Inclusion, Equity, and Community":mailto:l60qmlb
 93d9qlrf78jk9i21bms@group.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260814T161610
END:VEVENT
