BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ot433qfpn068rjfq2qjtcu8kvs_20280502T170000Z
SEQUENCE:0
DTSTAMP:20260924T045925
DTSTART:20280502T120000
DTEND:20280502T130000
SUMMARY:Caring for Aging Parents for Staff and Faculty
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
LOCATION:Multicultural Center 019
DESCRIPTION:<p class="cvGsUA direction-ltr align-start para-style-body"><s
 pan class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature
 -calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Navigating the com
 plexities of eldercare—from managing </span><span class="a_GcMg font-fea
 ture-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-
 none text-strikethrough-none">medical appointments and legal paperwork to 
 the emotional </span><span class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-featur
 e-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-n
 one">weight of changing family roles—is a journey few of us are prepared
  for. Whether you are currently providing daily care for an aging parent\,
  supporting an adult friend through a health crisis\, or simply beginning 
 to plan for the future\, you don't have to manage it in isolation. </span>
 </p>\n<p class="cvGsUA direction-ltr align-start para-style-body"><span cl
 ass="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-
 off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none">We hope to provide a ded
 icated space where we can find both practical resources and authentic peer
  support. By coming together\, we can share vetted local resources\, navig
 ate insurance and healthcare hurdles\, and offer a listening ear to those 
 balancing professional excellence with personal sacrifice.</span></p>\n\n<
 ul>\n 	<li><span class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off
  font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Resou
 rce Sharing: </span><span class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature
 -clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-no
 ne">Access to curated lists of local home-health services\, elder law spec
 ialists\, and respite care.</span></li>\n 	<li><span class="a_GcMg font-fe
 ature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration
 -none text-strikethrough-none">Regular Meet-ups: </span><span class="a_GcM
 g font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-d
 ecoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Informal gatherings to discuss cha
 llenges and successes.</span></li>\n 	<li><span class="a_GcMg font-feature
 -liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-decoration-none
  text-strikethrough-none">Expert Guest Speakers: </span><span class="a_GcM
 g font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-calt-off text-d
 ecoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Occasional sessions with professio
 nals in gerontology\, financial planning\, and mental health.</span></li>\
 n</ul>\n<p class="cvGsUA direction-ltr align-start para-style-body"><span 
 class="a_GcMg font-feature-liga-off font-feature-clig-off font-feature-cal
 t-off text-decoration-none text-strikethrough-none">Taking care of those w
 ho once took care of us is a profound responsibility\, but it can also be 
 an exhausting one. We invite you to join us for our inaugural meeting to h
 elp shape this group into a community that truly serves your needs. Togeth
 er\, we can ensure that as we care for others\, we are also caring for our
 selves.</span></p>\n\nView this event on the Carleton College website:\nht
 tps://www.carleton.edu/_c/rn1B
ORGANIZER;CN="Carleton Staff Events":mailto:lh1jd4felv7e6i55jm72gadrgo@gro
 up.calendar.google.com
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260604T143224
END:VEVENT
